This repository contains files from other projects:

- Tiny Tapeout Verilog template for IHP (Tiny Tapeout, Apache-2.0):
  .github/workflows/docs.yaml, fpga.yaml, gds.yaml, test.yaml; .devcontainer/; test/Makefile and test/tb.v
  (both modified); info.yaml and docs/info.md (filled in).
- Tiny Tapeout SRAM example (https://github.com/ttcodebot/ttihp-cmos5l-sram-example), Apache-2.0:
  src/sram_bb.v, src/pdn_cfg.tcl (LibreLane contributors, Efabless Corporation), librelane_plugin_sram_pdn.py,
  odb_stripes.py (Ken Pettit, https://github.com/kdp1965/ihp-um-janestreet-prism; modified here, see the file).
- IHP Open PDK (https://github.com/IHP-GmbH/IHP-Open-PDK), Apache-2.0, Copyright IHP PDK Authors:
  the behavioural SRAM models in src/rsoc8/tb/ihp/ and test/sram_model/. The hardened layout and the layout of
  the clock macro in analog/ contain cells and devices of this PDK.

Compiled firmware images (test/fw/uart_echo.hex, and the images that the test scripts build) contain the
start-up code of the C library avr-libc (crtattiny40.o), which is distributed under the BSD-3-Clause licence.
Its copyright notice, conditions and disclaimer are in LICENSES/avr-libc-copyright.txt.

The images also contain routines of the GCC runtime library (libgcc), which is distributed under the GNU
General Public License version 3 with the GCC Runtime Library Exception. The exception permits distributing
the compiled images under other terms.
